>> MF=5 ENERGY DISTRIBUTIONS OF SECONDARY PARTICLES               9228 1451  633
                                                                  9228 1451  634
MT=18 PROMPT FISSION NEUTRON SPECTRUM MATRIX                      9228 1451  635
   Prompt fission neutron spectrum matrix for the n + 235U system 9228 1451  636
was calculated (Ma03) using the Los Alamos (Madland-Nix) model    9228 1451  637
(MN82) in its exact formulation with energy-dependent compound    9228 1451  638
nucleus formation cross sections for the inverse processes. The   9228 1451  639
matrix includes first-, second-, and third-chance fission         9228 1451  640
components and also includes the neutrons evaporated prior to     9228 1451  641
fission in second- and third-chance fission. The tabulated        9228 1451  642
distribution law (LF=1) is used.                                  9228 1451  643
   The matrix is calculated for 19 incident neutron energies.     9228 1451  644
These are:                                                        9228 1451  645
     0.0, 0.5, 1.0, 1.5, 2.0, 2.5, 3.0, 4.0, 5.0, 6.0, 7.0, 8.0,  9228 1451  646
     9.0, 10.0, 11.0, 12.0, 13.0, 14.0, 15.0 MeV.                 9228 1451  647
   The 20-MeV spectrum is simply a duplication of the 15-MeV      9228 1451  648
spectrum.                                                         9228 1451  649
   Note that the thermal spectrum is identical to that of ENDF/B- 9228 1451  650
VI. This is due to the fact that the two most recent differential 9228 1451  651
measurements of the thermal spectrum and the most accepted set of 9228 1451  652
integral cross section measurements in the thermal spectrum       9228 1451  653
constitute three mutually incompatible experimental sets. This    9228 1451  654
incompatibility has yet to be resolved.                           9228 1451  655
                                                                  9228 1451  656
MT=455 DELAYED NEUTRON EMISSION SPECTRA FROM FISSION              9228 1451  657
   The abundances are based on the new delayed-neutron            9228 1451  658
calculations (Wi05) described under MF=1, MT=455. However, the    9228 1451  659
earlier six-group spectra from ENDF/B-VI are carried over to      9228 1451  660
ENDF/B-VII because new multigroup spectra have not yet been       9228 1451  661
calculated with the new library.                                  9228 1451  662
